			"notes": "Extended ore support!\n\n![Mekanism & ImEng samples](images/new%20samples.png)\n\nNew Content:\n- Added support for Immersive Engineering ores\n    - Nickel, Lead, Silver, Alumin(i)um, and Uranium all have stony, sandy, and red sandy samples\n- Added support for Mekanism ores\n    - Osmium, Fluorite, and Uranium (shared with Immersive Engineering) also all have stony, sandy, and red sandy samples\n    - I learned that I cannot spell fluorite correctly without a lot of effort. Flourite.\n- Added flint sample for use in modpacks\n    - They drop one flint\n    - I am not entirely happy with the texture, might revisit it later\n\nTweaks:\n- Reduced redstone powder drop to a max of 3 per sample\n- Nether quartz ore samples now drop between 0 and 1 nether quartz, enabling use without forcing use of Sky's Overworld Quartz\n- Added stonecutting recipe to turn an andesite block into andesite samples, now you can have placeable stones!\n\nFixes:\n- Fixed an interaction between Large Ore Deposits, Surface Samples, and Snow! Real Magic where an unknown sample type generated above a deposit would become entombed in snow and never update its model\n- Added suspicious sand to the list of blocks that trigger variant changes\n\nThis is a 1.21 release"
		},
